00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:16.600
He said, you see, all those questions, I said, the only thing that you really were interested

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:19.540
That's why they go

00:19:19.540 --> 00:19:23.560
You have either a brother

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:24.960
Or

00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:27.320
A father or a brother

00:19:27.320 --> 00:19:34.880
But no man and I don't need

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:36.620
And we responded

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:44.040
We have an old father

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:46.100
And a child

00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:48.920
who is, was born in his old age.

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:51.700
Mind you, that doesn't say Zekunim huloh.

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:55.040
Because in Joseph, that was Zekunim huloh

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:57.320
in the sense that he was intelligent.

00:19:57.480 --> 00:19:59.740
The words Aken, he says Aken, she's going to have fun.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.080
He has been Zekunim.

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:01.980
All right.

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:06.800
And, and Ahim met.

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:10.140
He has only one brother

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:13.000
and he's from his mother's side.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:16.280
and this brother had died

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:21.120
he's the only one

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:24.740
that remained from that mother

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:27.060
the Aviv at home

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:29.940
and his father loved him

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:32.520
he did change all of it

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:36.020
he understands that sometimes

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:39.320
an older man has a preference

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:40.640
for his younger child

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:43.620
they no longer get angry at that

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:45.240
as they were angry at Joseph

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:47.960
he also understands

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:50.240
that sometimes

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:51.780
somebody

00:20:51.780 --> 00:20:53.440
loves

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:55.360
a son

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:57.220
more than another son

00:20:57.220 --> 00:20:59.980
it doesn't mean because

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:01.480
I love Benjamin

00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:03.180
that I don't love you too

00:21:03.180 --> 00:21:05.840
and so on

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:08.000
now they understand

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:09.320
that you see

00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:11.620
and they speak it in a normal way.

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:13.320
Ve'aviv ahevo

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:15.980
v'atomer el'avadecha

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:17.540
And you

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:19.240
said to us

00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:22.040
Holidum hu el'ayim

00:21:22.040 --> 00:21:26.980
Bring him to me.

00:21:30.980 --> 00:21:32.780
Va'asimah eni alayim

00:21:32.780 --> 00:21:33.980
No.

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:36.520
What does it mean?

00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:38.260
Va'asimah eni alayim

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:45.260
Let's see who knows Arabic. I'm not going to ask this kids that just came from Syria because they really know Arabic only from the street.

00:21:45.260 --> 00:21:50.260
But, let's see, what does it mean in Arabic, anayati?

00:21:54.260 --> 00:21:59.260
Say, Al-Yaghaon says, I need, like anayati in Arabic.

00:21:59.260 --> 00:22:05.260
Anayati means, I'm going to help my prophetess. I'm going to take care of him.

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:09.780
I am going to watch over him

00:22:09.780 --> 00:22:12.140
you know what I am going to watch over him

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:16.420
this child has a diplomatic passport

00:22:16.420 --> 00:22:19.600
he has diplomatic immunity

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:21.300
you called him

00:22:21.300 --> 00:22:23.220
you told him to come

00:22:23.220 --> 00:22:24.760
he didn't want to come

00:22:24.760 --> 00:22:28.440
and therefore by calling him here

00:22:28.440 --> 00:22:31.460
you are saying

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:33.820
if the president of Russia

00:22:33.820 --> 00:22:36.780
tells me to come to Russia,

00:22:38.280 --> 00:22:39.760
I have diplomatic immunity.

00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:43.460
He invited me. I am his guest.

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:52.060
And now it is true that he did something wrong.

00:22:52.060 --> 00:22:54.220
All right?

00:22:54.900 --> 00:22:56.500
But there is a solution to that.

00:22:57.100 --> 00:22:58.100
All right? Now.

00:22:59.580 --> 00:23:03.060
But I want you to see how precise

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:09.760
every turn in the Torah is. Alright?

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:24.780
Sorry, even with your protection we cannot do that because this child

00:23:24.780 --> 00:23:35.300
cannot abandon his father. Do you know why? Because if he will abandon his father,

00:23:35.300 --> 00:23:45.360
his father will die. We will be killing our father. And therefore even with your kind

00:23:45.360 --> 00:23:55.200
diplomatic assurances were refused. And then in an unusual manner

00:24:00.880 --> 00:24:05.520
This is a sine qua non. If your brother doesn't come here,

00:24:05.520 --> 00:24:09.920
I am not going to allow you to be here. You shall not see my face.

00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:12.420
In other words, you cannot come here.

00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:13.560
Alright?

00:24:15.560 --> 00:24:20.060
وَهِكْ يَعَلِينُ الْعَبْدِخَا عَبِينُ مَنَا كَتْلُؤِتْ دِبْرِيَةٌ لِي

00:24:20.060 --> 00:24:20.980
Interesting.

00:24:21.220 --> 00:24:31.060
You know, these brothers who were deniers, liars, good joints, suffering.

00:24:31.980 --> 00:24:32.380
You know what?

00:24:32.840 --> 00:24:35.840
Now you see that they have to wear the same shoes.

00:24:35.840 --> 00:24:37.300
You know, the line.

00:24:37.780 --> 00:24:38.800
I mean, they're open.

00:24:38.800 --> 00:24:42.600
big change, it was a total metamorphosis in them. Right?

00:24:42.600 --> 00:24:49.000
When we went to our father and we told your words,

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:55.400
please buy us some food, and we told them,

00:24:55.400 --> 00:24:59.400
we cannot go to Egypt,

00:24:59.400 --> 00:25:08.700
we cannot come and see this man without your son Benjamin.

00:25:08.700 --> 00:25:17.080
they accept the fact

00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:20.420
my father says you know that my wife

00:25:20.420 --> 00:25:23.560
gave birth to two children

00:25:23.560 --> 00:25:26.720
this was part of the whole problem

00:25:26.720 --> 00:25:30.100
at one time they were angry

00:25:30.100 --> 00:25:31.040
they were jealous

00:25:31.040 --> 00:25:33.380
they were angry and jealous because

00:25:33.380 --> 00:25:35.440
because

00:25:35.440 --> 00:25:37.360
Jacob

00:25:37.360 --> 00:25:40.760
loved Rachel more than anybody else.

00:25:41.560 --> 00:25:45.780
And now Jacob is saying, Rachel is my wife.

00:25:46.440 --> 00:25:48.260
You know why Rachel is my wife?

00:25:48.800 --> 00:25:52.440
Because he married whomever he married afterwards.

00:25:53.080 --> 00:25:55.480
You know why he married whoever he married afterwards?

00:25:56.280 --> 00:25:58.300
Because of Rachel.

00:25:58.800 --> 00:26:01.520
He never married Leah because he loved Leah.

00:26:01.920 --> 00:26:03.520
He never wanted Leah.

00:26:04.020 --> 00:26:06.960
What he wanted was Rachel.

00:26:07.360 --> 00:26:32.040
And now there is finally these children are mature. These children become men. And they realized that the father was right. That somehow the grandpa Laban had brought about a situation which is abnormal.

00:26:32.040 --> 00:26:36.000
and now what is important for us

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:37.020
to understand this

00:26:37.020 --> 00:26:41.960
is that precisely the strong force

00:26:41.960 --> 00:26:45.180
in their life what made them angry

00:26:45.180 --> 00:26:48.320
and made them want to kill one another

00:26:48.320 --> 00:26:51.240
now they accept it as fact

00:26:51.240 --> 00:26:53.220
they are no longer angry

00:26:53.220 --> 00:26:56.180
you see they accepted this

00:26:56.180 --> 00:26:58.640
again you see the metamorphosis

00:26:58.640 --> 00:27:06.460
The change taking place. How these people are becoming more and more humane.

00:27:07.020 --> 00:27:14.720
Alright? Now, verse 28.

00:27:16.020 --> 00:27:19.740
Still they are quoting what Yaakov told them.

00:27:20.740 --> 00:27:22.360
By Yeseha I had the etiv.

